#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:1264
msgid "HTML page cache"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:169
msgid "Stores eligible public HTML responses in Redis through advanced-cache.php. No cached pages are written to disk."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:174
msgid "Enable page cache"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:174
msgid "The plugin attempts to add define( 'WP_CACHE', true ); to wp-config.php when needed. If automatic enabling fails, set WP_CACHE to true manually and verify the Status tab."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:175
msgid "Page TTL"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:176
msgid "CDN cache lifetime"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:176
msgid "Seconds a CDN or reverse proxy may keep a cache hit, sent as Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, s-maxage=N. Browsers still revalidate every time. Zero disables the header, which is what shared caches see today. Enable this only if you are willing to purge the CDN when content changes, because the CDN does not know about page invalidation."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:177
msgid "Clear a page's cache when it is updated"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:177
msgid "Invalidates the updated, published, unpublished, scheduled or deleted post, page or custom post type and all translations detected through WPML or Polylang. Listing pages are handled by the option below."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:178
msgid "Clear related taxonomy archives when a post is updated"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:178
msgid "Invalidates archives of current, previous and new assigned terms in public standard and custom taxonomies, including hierarchical parents and terms assigned to WPML or Polylang translations, and the archive of a term that is renamed or deleted. Unrelated taxonomy archives remain cached."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:179
msgid "Clear listing pages when content is published"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:179
msgid "When public content is published, changed, unpublished, scheduled or deleted, invalidates the front page, the posts page, post type, author and date archives, search results and cached 404 pages, with all their pagination. Taxonomy archives use the option above when it is enabled, and this one otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:180
msgid "Clear the page cache when the site changes"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:180
msgid "Clears the whole HTML page cache after menus, widgets, Customizer settings, the active theme, core site settings, ACF options pages or a plugin, theme or core update change. Deploys that bypass WordPress can run: wp simple-redis-cache purge page"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:181
msgid "Cache logged-in users"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:181
msgid "Disabled is safest. Logged-in variants are isolated by session when enabled."
msgstr ""

