#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:773
msgid "Only needed if Cloudflare also caches your HTML pages. Cloudflare builds its cache key from the method, host and URL — cookies are not part of it — so a page stored for an anonymous visitor is served to logged-in users too. That request never reaches WordPress, so no setting in this plugin, including Cache logged-in users, can prevent it. The expression below keeps such visitors out of the rule."
